silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_24_rosetta_stone_cross_domain_sections_06_six_step_scaffold_exposition_concrete_anchor_6#yonedalemma_s620 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.24_rosetta_stone_cross_domain.sections.06_six_step_scaffold_exposition.concrete_anchor_6#yonedalemma_s620" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_24_rosetta_stone_cross_domain_sections_06_six_step_scaffold_exposition_concrete_anchor_6#yonedalemma_s620 silm:hasLongDescription "The YonedaLemma_S620 is the Yoneda lemma (JoC 6.20): an object is determined by its representable profile; all five domain readings produce the same profile so they identify the same apex. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'YonedaLemma_S620', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
